<p><strong>What this page is.</strong> An inventory of every BFI mobile app and web application we could find, with its GitHub repository, stack, where it runs, and who it is for. Built on 20 October 2026 from four sources, cross-checked against each other. Each row says how sure we are.</p><h2>Summary</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Mobile apps in the stores: 7.</strong> Six are Flutter apps built from three repositories in <code>bfi-finance</code>. One (M-Beat, employee learning) has no repository in the org and is probably a vendor product.</p></li><li><p><strong>Web applications: about 60 runnable, not archived</strong>, from 280 repositories in the org. 43 are React single-page apps. The rest: the Next.js corporate site, a Strapi CMS, two PHP public sites, two HTMX back offices for LORA, and 17 small PHP tools for the PMO.</p></li><li><p><strong>Two deployment worlds.</strong> The legacy <code>ms-bfi-*</code> web UIs each have a Helm chart in <code>bfi-app-deployment</code> with a hostname we can read. The Bravo and LORA frontends are static builds pushed to Google Cloud Storage by their own GitHub workflows; the only place they appear in the manifests is as allowed origins on the API gateway.</p></li><li><p><strong>One framework family.</strong> React everywhere on the web (versions 17, 18 and 19 side by side), Flutter everywhere on mobile. No Vue, Angular, React Native or native Kotlin/Swift apps.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ownership is concentrated.</strong> The GitHub team <code>tribe-bravo-leads</code> holds about 45 of the frontend repositories, including both main Flutter apps.</p></li></ul><h2>Assessments</h2><p>One assessment page per store app, each a child of this page. Every assessment compares the app with the DK Jago app and ends in a roadmap ordered by risk to users.</p><ul><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="BFI Mobile App Assessment" ri:version-at-save="20" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[BFI Mobile App Assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="Genfi mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="4" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[Genfi mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="MyShaf mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="3" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[MyShaf mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="Square mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="4" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[Square mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="MY BISPRO mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="3" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[MY BISPRO mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li></ul><p>Roadmaps: the BFI customer app has its own. The four agency apps share the phases that touch the monorepo and keep per-app pages for approved deltas, the pilot feature and the remaining features.</p><ul><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="Mobile roadmap: step by step" ri:version-at-save="8" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[Mobile roadmap: step by step]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="Agency apps roadmap: shared phases" ri:version-at-save="2" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[Agency apps roadmap: shared phases]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="GENFI roadmap: step by step" ri:version-at-save="2" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[GENFI roadmap: step by step]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="SQUARE roadmap: step by step" ri:version-at-save="2" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[SQUARE roadmap: step by step]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li></ul><h2>Assessments</h2><p>One assessment page per store app, each a child of this page. Every assessment compares the app with the DK Jago app and ends in a roadmap ordered by risk to users.</p><ul><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="BFI Mobile App Assessment" ri:version-at-save="20" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[BFI Mobile App Assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="Genfi mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="4" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[Genfi mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="MyShaf mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="3" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[MyShaf mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="Square mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="4" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[Square mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="MY BISPRO mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="3" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[MY BISPRO mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="myBRO (RO Tools) mobile app assessment" ri:version-at-save="3" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[myBRO (RO Tools) mobile app assessment]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li></ul><p>Roadmaps: the BFI customer app has its own. The four agency apps share the phases that touch the monorepo and keep per-app pages for approved deltas, the pilot feature and the remaining features.</p><ul><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="Mobile roadmap: step by step" ri:version-at-save="8" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[Mobile roadmap: step by step]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="Agency apps roadmap: shared phases" ri:version-at-save="2" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[Agency apps roadmap: shared phases]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="GENFI roadmap: step by step" ri:version-at-save="2" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[GENFI roadmap: step by step]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li><li><p><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title="SQUARE roadmap: step by step" ri:version-at-save="2" /><ac:plain-text-link-body><![CDATA[SQUARE roadmap: step by step]]></ac:plain-text-link-body></ac:link></p></li></ul><h2>How we built the list</h2><table data-table-width="1800" data-layout="full-width"><thead><tr><th><p>Source</p></th><th><p>What it gives</p></th><th><p>What it misses</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>GitHub org <code>bfi-finance</code> (280 repos, by language and <code>package.json</code>/<code>pubspec.yaml</code>)</p></td><td><p>Every repository and its stack</p></td><td><p>Whether the app is deployed or used</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Helm manifests (<code>bfi-app-deployment</code>, <code>app-deployment</code>, <code>origin/master</code> 20 Oct)</p></td><td><p>Hostnames, environments, public or private, image names</p></td><td><p>Static frontends deployed to GCS</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Gateway CORS lists (<code>krakend-gateway</code> values)</p></td><td><p>Hostnames of web apps that call the API</p></td><td><p>Which repo builds each hostname</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>App Store lookup, Google Play search, Datadog RUM application list (60 apps)</p></td><td><p>What is live in users' hands and being monitored</p></td><td><p>RUM IDs are injected at build time, so the mapping to a repo is by name</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Repository URLs all follow <code>https://github.com/bfi-finance/&lt;repo&gt;</code>. &quot;Last push&quot; is the last commit date on GitHub as of 20 October 2026.</p><h2>Mobile apps</h2><h3>In the stores</h3><table data-table-width="1800" data-layout="full-width"><thead><tr><th><p>Store name</p></th><th><p>Package / bundle id</p></th><th><p>Repo (app folder)</p></th><th><p>Audience</p></th><th><p>iOS</p></th><th><p>Andro