d><p>Branch management</p></td><td><p>Not matched</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>sa-tools.bfi.co.id</p></td><td><p><code>ms-sa-tools</code></p></td><td><p>Private</p></td><td><p>Internal tools</p></td><td><p>Not matched</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>formio-attachment.bfi.co.id</p></td><td><p><code>bfi-formio-ui</code></p></td><td><p>Both ingresses disabled in prod</p></td><td><p>Forms</p></td><td><p>Not matched</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>iad-sandbox-army.prod.bfi.co.id</p></td><td><p><code>army</code></p></td><td><p>Private</p></td><td><p>Internal audit</p></td><td><p>Not matched</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>s1.bfi.co.id</p></td><td><p><code>strategyone-*</code></p></td><td><p>Private, internal gateway</p></td><td><p>Risk decisioning (StrategyOne, vendor)</p></td><td><p>Vendor product</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>e-pmo.prod.bfi.co.id/pmotools, /pmotools2</p></td><td><p><code>pmotools</code>, <code>pmotools2</code></p></td><td><p>Private</p></td><td><p>PMO</p></td><td><p><code>pmo-pmotools</code>, <code>pmo-pmotools2</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Non-prod only: frp, dga, ticketing, engineering-report, redash, autiq, pmo-omega, promesys</p></td><td><p>various</p></td><td><p>Private</p></td><td><p>Internal</p></td><td><p>Partly matched (<code>pmo-promesys</code>)</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Internal: decision management and other hosts behind the internal gateway</h3><p>Seen as allowed origins on <code>krakend-gateway-internal</code> (SSO through the google-workspace realm). No chart or repo was matched for these: <code>da-obligor</code>, <code>dm-afrules</code>, <code>dm-aggregation</code>, <code>dm-mdata</code>, <code>dm-rules</code>, <code>webcore5</code>, <code>webcore6</code> (all <code>.bfi.co.id</code>, mostly plain HTTP). Likely legacy decision-management and core web apps. Also seen in service config, unmatched: <code>xportal-app.bfi.co.id</code>, <code>ca.bfi.co.id</code>, <code>orientasi.*</code>, <code>genfi.*.bravo</code>.</p><h3>PMO tools (17 small PHP apps)</h3><p>Repos <code>pmo-absen</code>, <code>pmo-actionlog</code>, <code>pmo-boarding</code>, <code>pmo-briliance</code>, <code>pmo-core</code>, <code>pmo-dfr</code>, <code>pmo-kboard</code>, <code>pmo-momo</code>, <code>pmo-pdc</code>, <code>pmo-pmotools</code>, <code>pmo-pmotools2</code>, <code>pmo-projo</code>, <code>pmo-promesys</code>, <code>pmo-rapi</code>, <code>pmo-resep</code>, <code>pmo-room</code>, <code>pmo-vms</code>. Plain PHP (no <code>composer.json</code>), last pushes between Aug 2024 and Feb 2026. Only <code>pmotools</code>, <code>pmotools2</code> (prod) and <code>promesys</code>, <code>pmo-omega</code> (dev) have charts. Whether the others are live is not known.</p><h3>Web libraries, templates and login themes (not apps)</h3><table data-table-width="1800" data-layout="full-width"><thead><tr><th><p>Repo</p></th><th><p>What it is</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><code>frontend-ui</code></p></td><td><p><code>@bfi-finance/frontend-ui</code>, web design system</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>frontend-kit</code></p></td><td><p>Shared config</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>bravo-voyagers</code></p></td><td><p>Unified navigation shell component</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>bfi-ai-chat-sdk</code></p></td><td><p><code>@bfi-finance/chat-sdk</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>bravo-image-validation-web-sdk</code></p></td><td><p>Web image validation SDK</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>bravo-eslint-config</code>, <code>bravo-prettier-config</code></p></td><td><p>Lint and format config</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>bravo-react-ts-boilerplate</code></p></td><td><p>React template. At least 12 apps still carry its default package name</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>agency-spvcockpit-login</code>, <code>bravo-ims-login</code>, <code>bravo-repeat-order-web-tele-login</code>, <code>bravo-surveyor-console-login</code>, <code>dms-edoc-login</code></p></td><td><p>Keycloak login themes</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>bravo-unsecuredv2-web-lib</code></p></td><td><p>Archived</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>bravo-monorepo-egc-fe</code>, <code>bravo-repeat-order-cre-tool-app</code></p></td><td><p>Empty repos</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><code>lora-template-builder-poc</code>, <code>doc-renderer-builder</code>, <code>dashboard-otrs</code></p></td><td><p>Proof of concept and internal tools (React 19 / Astro)</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Observations</h2><ul><li><p><strong>The mobile estate is 3 repos and 6 apps.</strong> The agency monorepo alone ships four store apps. Any mobile platform decision (RASP, design system, CI) should be made for all three repos, not only <code>bravo-customer-app</code>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Three React majors in production.</strong> React 17 lives in the LMS apps, the underwriting console, the NDF apps and the customer platform. React 18 is the default. React 19 is only in the corporate site. Vite ranges from 3 to 8. The web estate has no shared upgrade cadence.</p></li><li><p><strong>Monitoring gaps.</strong> SQUARE's RUM events are not processed. MY BISPRO and M-Beat have no RUM app. Five web RUM apps are inactive. About 12 web repos have no Datadog package at all.</p></li><li><p><strong>Deployment is not visible for most Bravo frontends.</strong> They go to GCS buckets through per-repo workflows and a shared <code>bfi-base-template</code> workflow. There is no single place that lists which bucket serves which hostname. That is why about 20 hostnames on this page have no confirmed repo and about 25 repos have no confirmed hostname.</p></li><li><p><strong>Legacy charts without repos.</strong> About 12 <code>ms-bfi-*</code> charts in <code>bfi-app-deployment</code> have no matching frontend repo in the org. Either the source is in another org or forge (two repos mention a GitLab migration), or the image is built from a repo with a different name.</p></li><li><p><strong>Archived but still referenced.</strong><code>bravo-eline-portal-fe</code> is archived, yet <code>prod-eline-portal</code> is an active RUM app. Worth checking what still serves it.</p></li></ul><h2>What we could not verify</h2><ul><li><p>Google Play update dates and install counts. Play pages did not return content to our tools.</p></li><li><p>Which hostnames are truly internet-reachable. &quot;Public&quot; and &quot;private&quot; above come from the ingress class, not from a network test.</p></li><li><p>The repo behind each GCS-hosted hostname. The bucket names live in each repo's workflow and in Terraform, which we did not read.</p></li><li><p>The second Datadog server was not queried. RUM apps that exist only there are missing.</p></li><li><p>Whether &quot;BFI PAS!&quot; is the old customer app, and what &quot;SMART Mobile - Collection&quot; is.</p></li><li><p>Whether any BFI apps still live only in GitLab.</p></li></ul><h2>How to keep this page current</h2><ul><li><p>A new frontend repo in <code>bfi-finance</code> should be added here with its hostname and RUM app on the day it first deploys.</p></li><li><p>The repo listing can be regenerated with <code>gh repo list bfi-finance --limit 1000 --json name,description,primaryLanguage,isArchived,pushedAt</code>. The store list comes from the iTunes lookup API for developer id 1495767927. The RUM list comes from Datadog.</p></li></ul>